.TH SDL_AppResult 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_AppResult \- Return values for optional main callbacks.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_init.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef enum SDL_AppResult
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_APP_CONTINUE,   /**< Value that requests that the app continue from the main callbacks. */
.BI "    SDL_APP_SUCCESS,    /**< Value that requests termination with success from the main callbacks. */
.BI "    SDL_APP_FAILURE     /**< Value that requests termination with error from the main callbacks. */
.BI "} SDL_AppResult;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Returning
.BR SDL_APP_SUCCESS
or
.BR SDL_APP_FAILURE
from
.BR SDL_AppInit ,
.BR SDL_AppEvent ,
or
.BR SDL_AppIterate
will terminate the program and report success/failure to the operating system\[char46] What that means is platform-dependent\[char46] On Unix, for example, on success, the process error code will be zero, and on failure it will be 1\[char46] This interface doesn\(aqt allow you to return specific exit codes, just whether there was an error generally or not\[char46]
.PP
Returning
.BR SDL_APP_CONTINUE
from these functions will let the app continue to run\[char46]
.PP
See
.URL https://wiki.libsdl.org/SDL3/README-main-functions#main-callbacks-in-sdl3 "Main callbacks in SDL3"
for complete details\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This enum is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

